course: dictionary
lesson: 13008
title: Extinguished: put out or ended
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Extinguished is a word you will meet in fire safety lessons and in stories. It means put out, so a fire or light stops burning or shining. It is the past form of the verb extinguish, which also appears as extinguishes and extinguishing.
explain: Look at the clues around it. «The firefighters sprayed water, and at last the fire was extinguished.» Fire burns, water is sprayed on it, so extinguished must mean put out. Try your meaning in the sentence: «the fire was put out» still makes sense.
explain: Extinguished can also mean ended completely, often in a story. «All hope was extinguished when the boat sank.» Hope cannot be put out like a fire, so here the word means gone for good. This is the formal meaning, so read the rest of the sentence carefully before you decide.
fact: Extinguished is the past form of the verb extinguish.
fact: «Extinguished» means put out, so a fire or light stops burning or shining.
fact: «Extinguished» can also mean ended or destroyed completely, as in «all hope was extinguished».
fact: A fire extinguisher is a tool that puts out fires.
fact: Extinguished can also be an adjective, as in «the extinguished candle».
exercise: «The firefighters sprayed water, and at last the fire was extinguished.» What does extinguished mean? | Made bigger and brighter | Painted with bright colours | *Put out, so it stopped burning | Moved to another house
exercise: Which tool is used to put out a fire? | Fire alarm | *Fire extinguisher | Fire drill
exercise: «All hope was extinguished when the boat sank.» What does extinguished suggest here? | *Ended completely, gone for good | Made brighter and stronger | Found again after a search | Put neatly in a box
test: «The candle was extinguished with one puff.» What happened to the candle? | It grew taller | It was lit again | It was painted red | *It stopped burning
test: Which word is the past form of extinguish? | *extinguished | extinguish | extinguishes | extinguishing
exam: Maya says extinguished can mean put out or ended. Which sentence uses the second, formal meaning? | «The bonfire was extinguished with sand.» | «The fire was extinguished by the team.» | «The lamp was extinguished at night.» | *«Her last hope was extinguished.»
